\begin{align*}
(x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3 &= (2x - 10)^3 \\
(x^3 - 9x^2 + 27x - 27) + (x^3 - 21x^2 + 147x - 343) &= (8x^3 - 120x^2 + 600x - 1000) \\
2x^3 - 30x^2 + 174x - 370 &= 8x^3 - 120x^2 + 600x - 1000 \\
6x^3 - 90x^2 + 426x - 630 &= 0 \\
x^3 - 15x^2 + 71x - 105 &= 0.
\end{align*}
To find the roots, we look for factors of the constant term, $-105$, that add up to the coefficient of $x^2$, which is $-15$. The factors that satisfy this are $-1, -3, -5$. Thus, the equation can be factored as:
\begin{align*}
(x - 1)(x - 3)(x - 5) &= 0.
\end{align*}
